      <workList xml:id="workDesc_812d3dc9">
         <work xml:id="work_id58e8e98b">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_e387f8c9">B2:416</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_ida5bb86ae" xml:lang="it">Duetto </title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_7f1bbf70" xml:lang="it">Vincesti Adraste</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_820f5d88">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_id4f8d582a">Johann Adolph Scheibe </persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_id2c2f8740">
               <p xml:id="idm61">The Italian cantata on the king of Argos, Adraste (Adrasto), and presumably his victory in the second war of Thebes, includes a duet for two voices and strings which has not survived. However, information of its existence appears in the Breitkopf catalogue of 1761 suggesting that it might have been obtained from the estate of <persName xml:id="idm62" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName>, the cantor at Neukirche, Leipzig. It is also possible that Scheibe sent the work directly to the publishers. In 1765, it was listed in another of Breitkopf’s catalogues, this time also including an incipit. The work does not appear in the Breitkopf auction catalogue of 1836.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_97e0aff0">
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="biblList_212N200FA">
